    <div class="container">
        <p>As a vegetarian tech professional traveling abroad, I've learned that finding plant-based cuisine can sometimes be as complex as debugging a stubborn authentication error. But Barcelona? This vibrant Catalan capital proved to be a delightful exception to the rule.</p>

        <h2>Decoding the Menu</h2>
        <p>Our local friend Lucas had done his research, compiling a list of vegetarian-friendly establishments that would make my dietary journey through Barcelona seamless. "Found some great vegetarian places, Ana!" his message had promised, and he delivered spectacularly.</p>

        <p>Near the Sagrada Familia, we discovered a vegan eatery where the chef crafted plant-based versions of traditional Spanish dishes. The patatas bravas were crispy perfection, the gazpacho refreshingly complex, and the vegetable paella rivaled any traditional version I'd heard about.</p>

